## Course overview

History at Higher Level is the disciplined study of the past — and of how historians construct knowledge from incomplete, contested evidence. The course develops source-evaluation, argument, and the ability to weigh competing interpretations. Our focus is **20th-century world history**, with depth studies on the Cold War, authoritarian states, and decolonisation.

## What you will study

- **Prescribed subject** — *The move to global war*: Japanese, Italian, and German expansion in the 1930s.
- **World history topics** — authoritarian states (rise and rule), and the Cold War: superpower tensions and rivalries.
- **HL regional option** — selected depth studies in the history of Europe.

## Assessment

| Component | Weighting | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 | 20% | Source-based analysis |
| Paper 2 | 25% | Comparative essays |
| Paper 3 | 35% | Regional depth essays (HL) |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | Historical investigation |

## The Internal Assessment

The IA is a **2,200-word historical investigation** on a question of your choice. It includes an evaluation of two sources, your own analysis, and a reflection on the methods and limits of the historian's craft — a direct bridge to Theory of Knowledge.
